Let $X$ be a compact complex $3$-dimensional Kähler manifold such that $c_1(T_X)=0\in Pic(X)$ (hence by Yau theorem $X$ admits a Calabi-Yau metric). We can associate with $X$ several moduli spaces which have the virtual dimension zero:

a\) moduli of holomorphic curves in $X$ with fixed genus and degree;

b\) moduli of holomorphic vector bundles on $X$ (or, more generally, of coherent sheaves) with a fixed Chern character;

c\) moduli of special Lagrangian submanifolds[^1] with a fixed homology class endowed with a $U(1)$ local system.

